            <ArticleTitle>Rupture of an aneurysm of the ovarian artery following delivery and endovascular treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e7-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ajog.2008.04.053</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of spontaneous rupture of an ovarian artery aneurysm, 5 days after delivery. Severe abdominal pain justified a computed tomography scan, which revealed a massive retroperitoneal hematoma. Arteriography showed the rupture of an ovarian artery aneurysm that was successfully embolized using microcoils.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
